At Flix, we offer a dynamic work environment with competitive pay, strong growth opportunities, and a tech-driven approach to making travel more accessible, sustainable, and affordable. &nbsp;

We're looking for a motivated and driven Operations Manager (m/f/d) based in Lisbon area who will help us shape our team, drive the company to the next level, and have the most direct influence on our success.

About the Role

• You are responsible for managing all operational topics concerning Flixbus’ bus partners;

• Monitor and analyze KPIs to identify areas for improvement, providing actionable recommendations to enhance partner performance and service quality;

• You work hand on hand with other teams to build, maintain, and develop long-lasting partnerships with these Bus partners and Flix presence in bus stations, specifically in Porto area. Travelling within the country is expected at least once a month, most of the times with one overnight;

• You ensure compliance with Flixbus procedures and protocols, training, supporting, and developing the drivers of these Bus Partners and conduct regular inspections to ensure everything meets our quality standards;

• You will take responsibility for an accurate start of each new line and constant improvement of the quality of line operations, especially regarding fleet, drivers and punctuality;

• You take part in different cross-functional operational projects, including global driven ones;

• You provide, when required, field support with bus stations management, as well as with other structures located in travelling area (ex. ticketshops);

• Coordinate with internal teams (e.g., Line Planning, Business Development) to ensure seamless operations .

About You

• 3-6 years of work experience in operations (transportation) in Portugal and/or Spain or a dynamic daily environment (handling daily incoming requests) ability to adequately deal with different stakeholders (bus terminal managers, bus drivers, operations supervisors or regional authorities) with high social and negotiation skills;

• Trustworthiness, engagement, resourcefulness and flexibility, as well as a hands-on mentality. Independent, reliable and responsible working style;

• Organized and full respectful of the Flixbus processes and protocols;

• You are willing to travel at least monthly. most of the times with one overnight. Occasional international travelling (max. twice a year);

• Portuguese (native/proficient speaker level), highly fluent in English. Language skills&nbsp;will be tested. Spanish is a plus.

• Know how to motivate internal and external stakeholders, and how to prioritize and organize yourself between incoming daily requests and longer-term tasks.

We recognize that everyone carries a unique set of valuable skills and experiences. If you think you could have an impact even though you don't meet 100% of the requirements, we still encourage you to apply. We want to hear from you! &nbsp;

What We Offer

• Travel perks : 12 free Flix vouchers + 12 discount vouchers for friends &amp; family.&nbsp;

• Work from (M)Anywhere : Depending on your role, work from another location for up to 60 days per year.&nbsp;

• Hybrid work model : We are an office-first company, but we offer flexibility to balance work and life.&nbsp;

• Wellbeing support : Access confidential 1:1 counselling, courses, and stress management for yourself and up to four family members.&nbsp;

• Learning &amp; Development : Take advantage of language classes, training courses, and expert-led sessions to grow your skills.&nbsp;

• Mentoring Program : Connect with experienced colleagues to gain insights and accelerate your career.&nbsp;

